            <ArticleTitle>[Myocardial infarction complicating exercise test performed 72 hours after coronary angioplasty].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>99-103</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report a case of myocardial infarction complicating an exercise stress test performed 48 hours after successful angioplasty of a stenosed left anterior descending artery in a patient with unstable angina. Three similar cases have been previously reported. The probable mechanisms of coronary obstruction in this context are rupture of an atheromatous plaque, thrombosis and coronary spasm.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
